<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Classic of Poetry</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 11th–7th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a> · Also known as Shijing, Book of Songs, Book of Odes</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Classic of Poetry, or Shijing, is the oldest Chinese collection of poems, with 305 songs dating from the Western Zhou to the middle of the Spring and Autumn period. It includes folk songs from the states, court hymns and sacrificial odes. Traditionally said to have been edited by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/confucius">Confucius</a>, it became one of the Five Classics of Confucian learning.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/classic-of-poetry.jpg" alt="Classic of Poetry" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aethelwolf Emsworth. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%9C%A8%E9%90%B8_---_Confucian_wooden-clapper_bell.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
